{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2170-06-25 18:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, I’m Dr. Lee. I’ll be your doctor during this stay. Can you tell me what brought you in today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2170-06-25 18:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, Doctor. My legs have been swelling up more and more over the last two and a half weeks. It’s gone all the way up to my belly now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2170-06-25 18:37:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You’ve had lymphedema before, right? Has it been worse than usual?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2170-06-25 18:38:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’ve had it for years. But this time, even increasing my water pill didn’t help. I’ve gained about 10 pounds in a week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2170-06-25 18:39:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "And you’re on that 2-liter fluid limit and low-salt diet?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2170-06-25 18:40:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’ve been sticking to it. My primary doctor and I tried bumping up my Bumex, but nothing changed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2170-06-25 18:41:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. We’ll start IV furosemide to help reduce the swelling. We’ll also check your heart and rule out a blood clot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2170-06-25 18:42:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I had a PICC line placed last time. It’s still in my arm. Can we use that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2170-06-25 18:43:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll use it. We’ve already done a chest X-ray to confirm it’s in the right place—mid SVC, so it’s good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2170-06-25 18:44:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I don’t want it taken out. My veins are hard to access."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2170-06-25 18:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Understood. We’ll keep it for now, but we’ll talk later about long-term options like a port."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2170-06-25 18:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve also been wheezing a bit. Could that be related?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2170-06-25 18:47:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. Your lungs don’t show fluid on the X-ray, but we’ll monitor. You have a history of COPD, correct?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2170-06-25 18:48:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, and I know I should quit smoking. I’ve been trying."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2170-06-25 18:49:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great. We’ll give you support and resources. For now, we’ll start albuterol treatments as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2170-06-26 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs from last night look stable. Your kidney function is okay, and no signs of infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2170-06-26 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. My legs still hurt, though—especially the right shin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2170-06-26 09:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll get an ultrasound today to check for a blood clot. But your exam doesn’t suggest cellulitis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2170-06-26 09:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No redness or fever. Just a deep, throbbing pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2170-06-26 09:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Likely due to the swelling and stretch on the tissues. We can try gabapentin at night if you’re open to it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2170-06-26 09:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’d rather not. I’m already on a lot of meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2170-06-26 09:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Fair enough. We’ll focus on reducing the swelling first."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2170-06-27 11:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The ultrasound came back. No DVT in your right leg. Limited views of the calf, but no clot seen."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2170-06-27 11:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not a blood clot. That’s a relief."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2170-06-27 11:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Correct. We’ll keep you on IV lasix twice daily. Your weight’s down a little—good sign."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2170-06-27 11:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I can see my legs are a bit smaller. But I’m going to the bathroom a lot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2170-06-27 11:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s expected. We’re removing extra fluid. We’ll put in a catheter so you don’t have to keep getting up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2170-06-27 11:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’d prefer that. It’s hard to move with these swollen legs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2170-06-28 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. Your INR was low yesterday—1.8. We’ve increased your warfarin from 7mg to 9mg daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2170-06-28 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been on warfarin since my pulmonary embolism. I take it every day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2170-06-28 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. We’ll check again in a couple days to make sure it’s in range."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2170-06-28 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve noticed my mouth feels dry, and there’s white stuff on my tongue."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2170-06-28 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That could be thrush, especially with the diuretics drying you out. We’ll start nystatin mouthwash."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2170-06-28 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll use it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2170-06-29 07:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your Keppra level came back—19 mcg/mL. That’s in the therapeutic range."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2170-06-29 07:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been taking 1000mg twice a day, but my neurologist prescribed 1500. Should I increase it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2170-06-29 07:47:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Since your level is good and you haven’t had a seizure, we’ll keep it as is for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2170-06-29 07:48:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had non-epileptic episodes too, so it’s hard to tell."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2170-06-29 07:49:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll continue your current dose and follow up with neurology."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2170-06-30 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your creatinine has gone up to 1.5. That means we need to slow down the IV diuretics."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2170-06-30 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that bad? My kidneys?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2170-06-30 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s a sign we’re removing fluid too fast. We’ll stop IV lasix and restart your oral Bumex."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2170-06-30 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I’ll go back to my regular pill?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2170-06-30 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, 4mg daily. And we’ll keep you on fluid and salt restrictions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2170-07-01 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We noticed your urine is cloudy. We sent a culture. Could be a UTI from the catheter."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2170-07-01 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I haven’t felt any burning or urgency."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2170-07-01 08:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Sometimes with a catheter, symptoms are masked. We’ll wait for results before starting antibiotics."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2170-07-02 10:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your urine culture grew Citrobacter freundii. It’s sensitive to ciprofloxacin, so we’ll start that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2170-07-02 10:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that serious?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2170-07-02 10:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s a common bacteria in catheter infections. We’ll treat it for five days. We’ll also remove the catheter soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2170-07-02 10:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had it for a few days. I guess it makes sense."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2170-07-03 07:50:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your INR is now 2.6—perfect. You’ll go home on 9mg warfarin daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2170-07-03 07:51:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. I’ll keep my follow-up with my PCP for checks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2170-07-03 07:52:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Also, the rash under your left breast is looking better with the miconazole powder."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2170-07-03 07:53:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, less red and itchy. I’ll keep using it at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2170-07-04 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. Swelling’s improved, no more wheezing, and your labs are stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2170-07-04 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I go home tomorrow?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2170-07-04 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, if all goes well. We’ll discharge you with ciprofloxacin for five days and your regular meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2170-07-04 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the PICC line?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2170-07-04 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You can keep it, but we strongly recommend discussing a port or removal with your PCP."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2170-07-05 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re cleared to go home. We’ll review your discharge instructions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2170-07-05 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I feel much better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2170-07-05 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll continue Bumex, warfarin, and ciprofloxacin. Follow low salt and fluids—1500cc daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2170-07-05 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And see my primary doctor for follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2170-07-05 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and we strongly recommend you see a lymphedema clinic for long-term management."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2170-07-05 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll look into that. Thanks for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2170-07-05 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. Call if swelling worsens or you have fever, pain, or trouble breathing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 68,
      "time": "2170-07-05 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And I’ll try to quit smoking for good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 69,
      "time": "2170-07-05 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a great goal. We’re here to support you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 70,
      "time": "2170-07-05 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 71,
      "time": "2170-07-05 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nurse will bring your prescriptions and discharge papers shortly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 72,
      "time": "2170-07-05 09:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’m ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 73,
      "time": "2170-07-05 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll have your ride called. Take it easy, and follow up as scheduled."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 74,
      "time": "2170-07-05 09:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. Thank you again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 75,
      "time": "2170-07-05 09:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Get some rest and keep up the good work."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 76,
      "time": "2170-07-05 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 77,
      "time": "2170-07-05 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care, Ms. ___."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 78,
      "time": "2170-07-05 09:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "You too, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 79,
      "time": "2170-07-05 09:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nurse will assist you with discharge prep now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 80,
      "time": "2170-07-05 09:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Alright, I’ll wait for her."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 81,
      "time": "2170-07-05 09:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Have a safe trip home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 82,
      "time": "2170-07-05 09:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 83,
      "time": "2170-07-05 09:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll see you in follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 84,
      "time": "2170-07-05 09:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’ll make the appointments."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 85,
      "time": "2170-07-05 09:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Take care."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2170-06-25 18:29:00",
    "admission_end": "2170-07-05 19:38:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 58-year-old woman was admitted for acute worsening of chronic lower extremity lymphedema over 2.5 weeks, with significant swelling, weight gain, and discomfort. She was treated with IV furosemide via an existing PICC line, fluid and sodium restriction, and compression. Imaging confirmed no DVT, and her heart function remained stable. The hospital course was complicated by a catheter-associated UTI with Citrobacter freundii, treated with ciprofloxacin. Diuresis was limited by a rise in creatinine to 1.5, prompting transition back to oral bumetanide. Oral thrush and a candidal rash under the breast were treated with nystatin and miconazole. Her INR was optimized to 2.6 on warfarin 9mg daily. She improved clinically, with reduced edema and stable symptoms, and was discharged home on antibiotics, diuretics, and anticoagulation, with strong recommendations to follow up with primary care and a lymphedema clinic.",
    "problems": [
      "Other lymphedema",
      "Acute kidney failure, unspecified",
      "Candidiasis of mouth",
      "Body Mass Index 60.0-69.9, adult",
      "Urinary tract infection, site not specified",
      "Morbid obesity",
      "Infection and inflammatory reaction due to indwelling urinary catheter",
      "Urinary catheterization as the cause of abnormal reaction of patient, or of later complication, without mention of misadventure at time of procedure",
      "Candidiasis of skin and nails",
      "Disturbance of salivary secretion",
      "Other diuretics causing adverse effects in therapeutic use",
      "Tobacco use disorder",
      "Chronic obstructive asthma, unspecified",
      "Epilepsy, unspecified, without mention of intractable epilepsy",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Obstructive sleep apnea (adult)(pediatric)",
      "Unspecified acquired hypothyroidism",
      "Myalgia and myositis, unspecified",
      "Venous (peripheral) insufficiency, unspecified",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Other constipation",
      "Long-term (current) use of anticoagulants",
      "Personal history of venous thrombosis and embolism"
    ]
  }
}
